{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q30692905","formula":"C₂HNO","hill":"C2HNO","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":2.0,"H":1.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Formyl cyanide","ru":"Формилцианид"},"descriptions":{"en":"Formyl cyanide is a simple organic compound with the formula HCOCN and structure HC(=O)−C≡N. It is simultaneously a nitrile (R−C≡N) and an aldehyde (R−CH=O). Formyl cyanide is the simplest member of the acyl cyanide family. It is known to occur in space in the Sgr B2 molecular cloud.","ru":"Формилцианид (также цианоформальдегид, формилацетонитрил) — химическое соединение с химической формулой C2HNO. Формально можно считать и нитрилом и альдегидом. Формилцианид является простейшим представителем семейства ацилцианидов. Известно, что он встречается в космосе в молекулярном облаке Sgr B2."},"fame":6,"pubchemCid":3843063,"mass":55.04,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(=O)C#N","inchikey":"TUHMQDODLHWPCC-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"formyl cyanide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"3843063","atoms":5,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.631,"y":-0.384,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":1.755,"y":-0.191,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.758,"y":0.471,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":0.633,"y":0.104,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.968,"y":1.552,"z":0.001,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,2,2],[1,3,3],[2,3,1],[2,4,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q30692905","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Formyl_cyanide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A4%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BC%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%86%D0%B8%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B4","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"properties","name":"PubChem","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.n